"""Gateway between Git and MediaWiki: a git remote helper.

    git clone mw::https://example.com/wiki

This is a Python re-implementation of the Perl ``git-remote-mediawiki''.  It
speaks the MediaWiki Action API using nothing but the Python standard library.

Wiki pages are mapped to files named "<Page_title>.mw".  Each MediaWiki
revision becomes one Git commit on refs/mediawiki/<remote>/master, and the
MediaWiki revision id of each commit is recorded in a Git note in
refs/notes/<remote>/mediawiki so that later fetches know where to resume.

Configuration (all optional, see also README.org):

    remote.<name>.pages            space separated page titles to track
    remote.<name>.categories       space separated categories to track
    remote.<name>.namespaces       space separated namespaces to track
    remote.<name>.shallow          import only the last revision of each page
    remote.<name>.fetchStrategy    "by_page" (default) or "by_rev"
    remote.<name>.mediaimport      import media files on fetch (default false)
    remote.<name>.mediaexport      export media files on push (default true)
    remote.<name>.mwLogin          wiki user name (password via credential API)
    remote.<name>.mwPassword       wiki password (discouraged, use credentials)
    remote.<name>.mwDomain         wiki login domain (LDAP & friends)
    remote.<name>.dumbPush         do not update notes/refs on push
    mediawiki.fetchStrategy        fallback for remote.<name>.fetchStrategy
    mediawiki.dumbPush             fallback for remote.<name>.dumbPush
"""

